1441 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 471 0 R
/E (The Team Chat client renders incoming WebSocket messages by concatenating them into an innerHTML assignment without encoding. Both from and body originate from the server and reach the DOM as live markup. Because messages persist and are replayed through the same function when conversation history loads, injected script executes for every user who subsequently opens the conversation.)
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1442 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 471 0 R
/E (Note that all server-rendered values on this page are correctly escaped; only the WebSocket-delivered content is not, indicating the client-side render path was not treated as an output context.)
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1443 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 471 0 R
/E (The sender_name field is additionally reachable through the profile display name, which the server propagates to the messaging service. This provides a second-order injection path: a payload stored via /profile executes in a different component through a route the profile handler does not anticipate.)
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
