<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 475 0 R
/E (The application does not issue a new session identifier on successful authentication. The MRDSESSID value held before login remains in force afterwards, with the same identifier simply gaining authenticated status server-side. The login response sets mrd_prefs but returns no Set-Cookie for MRDSESSID.)
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1488 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 475 0 R
/E (An attacker who obtains a victim's pre-authentication session identifier therefore holds a valid authenticated session once the victim logs in, without ever learning their credentials. The application transmits all traffic in cleartext \(BB-20\) and contains three cross-site scripting findings \(BB-19\), so a pre-authentication identifier is obtainable by an on-path observer or through injected script.)
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
